Z||000014||deceler8||05-04-2000||06:02 PM||||Had to bring this topic up again...had a decklid that was really ugly...faded (almost white), cracks in the clearcoat...just assumed I'd take it off and have it painted.<P>So I took it off, wet sanded it down with 220, then 320, then 800, 1500 grits. I noticed that at no time did I ever remove any paint...<P>So I washed it off after sanding it, wiped it down with mineral spirits, and noticed while the spirits were wet that it shone like a brand new car. So I dried it off and sprayed it with one can of clear...then sanded that with 1500, then used compound...it looks like new. About a three foot deep shine. <P>Probably cost me all of $15 to do this...no reason why it wouldn't work on a hood or fender or other faded area. The key was that I never reached the layer of paint, even though I sanded pretty aggressively.||||reg||1
